Let $O$ denote an optimizer that has iterates $ m{	heta}_{t+1}\leftarrow m{	heta}_{t}-\alpha\mathbf{M}_{t}
abla f_{t}( m{	heta}_{t})$ when run on batch loss function $f_{t}( m{	heta})$ without weight decay, and $ m{	heta}_{t+1}\leftarrow(1-\lambda) m{	heta}_{t}-\alpha\mathbf{M}_{t}
abla f_{t}( m{	heta}_{t})$ when run on $f_{t}( m{	heta})$ with weight decay, respectively, with $\mathbf{M}_{t}
eq k\mathbf{I}$ (where $k\in\mathbb{R}$). Then, for $O$ there exists no L2 coefficient $\lambda^{\prime}$ such that running $O$ on batch loss $f^{	ext{reg}}_{t}( m{	heta})=f_{t}( m{	heta})+ rac{\lambda^{\prime}}{2}\left\lVert m{	heta}ightVert_{2}^{2}$ without weight decay is equivalent to running $O$ on $f_{t}( m{	heta})$ with decay $\lambda\in\mathbb{R}^{+}$.
